What this licence does and does not cover
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

It covers what is in this repository: the node itself (`Sources/`), its tests
(`Tests/`), the Swift client package (`Client/`), the build and setup scripts,
and the documentation under `Docs/` and `Skills/`.

It does not cover what a build pulls in. Thread resolves its dependencies at
build time and redistributes none of them here; each keeps its own licence.
The direct ones — swift-argument-parser, swift-crypto, swift-protobuf,
hummingbird, grpc-swift and its NIO transport and protobuf plugins — are
Apache-2.0.

`../Frigate` and `../Conduit` are sibling path dependencies, not vendored
sources: Thread requires a checkout of each beside it, and both are separately
licensed under their own terms. Conduit carries the `.proto` definitions and
generated stubs for the ThreadQuery, ThreadLibrary and ThreadGraph services;
Frigate carries the MLX stack used for on-device embeddings and graph
extraction.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Models
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No model weights are included in this repository. The on-device defaults
(`mlx-community/Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B-4bit-DWQ` for embeddings and
`mlx-community/Qwen3-1.7B-4bit` for graph extraction) are downloaded from the
Hugging Face Hub on first use and carry their own licences. The Mistral API
backends (`mistral-embed`, `mistral-tiny`) are a third-party hosted service
governed by Mistral's terms.

The Linux/CUDA build resolves a set of patched forks through Frigate —
`riteshpakala/mlx`, `mlx-swift`, `swift-transformers`, `mlx-swift-lm` and
`mlx.embeddings` — each a fork of its upstream project carrying CUDA and Linux
compatibility patches, and each remaining under the licence of the project it
forks. None of them are redistributed here; they are fetched at build time.
Docs/MLX-CUDA-Linux.md lists the branches and commit hashes.
